{"type":"text","timestamp":1794914698617,"sessionID":"ses_e16c18aa5ffeKftaTwAhrZX9BX","part":{"id":"prt_1e940bc6d00116YKDY11n0jOIj","messageID":"msg_1e940b93b001ehRmdVpMue9yng","sessionID":"ses_e16c18aa5ffeKftaTwAhrZX9BX","type":"text","text":"Upgrade done.\n\n**Changes**\n- `vendor/moneyfmt/__init__.py` — now byte-identical to the released `vendor-updates/moneyfmt-2.0.0/moneyfmt/__init__.py` (verified with `diff -r`).\n- `requirements.txt` — `moneyfmt==2.0.0`.\n- `invoicer/totals.py` — adapted to the 2.0.0 API: `MoneyError` → `MoneyFormatError` (invoicer/totals.py:8,30), `Line.amount`/`total()` are now `Decimal` (invoicer/totals.py:20,35), and `format_money(..., currency=CURRENCY)` passes the now keyword-only currency (invoicer/totals.py:42). `total()` seeds with `Decimal(\"0\")` so an empty invoice still renders `€0.00` as before.\n- `tests/test_moneyfmt_api.py` — new: pins the vendored version/pin, the rename, the Decimal-only and keyword-only contracts, an AST check that `invoicer/totals.py` never references removed names or calls `format_money` positionally, exact-decimal totals, and CLI stdout/stderr/exit-status contracts.\n\n**Verification**\n- `python -m unittest discover -s tests`: 17 tests, all pass (2 pre-existing + 15 new).\n- Replayed 32 CLI invocations before/after: 28 identical stdout+exit status. The only differences are the allowed one (exact decimals: `A=0.005 B=0.03` now totals €0.04 instead of €0.03) and NaN/Infinity inputs, where 2.0.0's new \"reject NaN/Infinity\" turns the old unhandled `decimal.InvalidOperation` traceback (exit 1) into a normal `error: cannot read amount 'NaN'` (exit 2) — that traceback could not be preserved anyway since it embedded the old vendored file's line numbers.\n- Mutation-checked the new tests: reverting the vendor copy, the rename, the keyword-only currency, or converting amounts back to float each makes the suite fail.","time":{"start":1794914696301,"end":1794914698615}}}
